---
source: crates/cartograph-cli/tests/frame.rs
expression: text(&o.stdout)
---
A codebase map with history.

Usage: cartograph [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init      Find the workspace, write cartograph.yaml, build the first index
  sync      Index the commits added since the last run
  status    Each repo's indexed commit, its HEAD and how far behind it is
  index     Index one repository's history (temporary single-repo form, IDX-07)
  verify    Compare fact hashes with another index or the manifest
  hooks     Install, remove or show the git hooks that sync after each commit
  schedule  Sync every workspace hourly, or stop doing so
  open      Serve the app on 127.0.0.1 and open it in the browser
  mcp       Run the MCP server over stdio
  tool      Run one MCP tool and print its JSON result
  impact    What a branch, a commit range or your uncommitted changes would affect
  check     Fail on stale corrections or broken architecture rules
  ask       Ask the map a question
  agents    Write MCP config for the coding agents on this machine
  doctor    Check the setup and print the command that fixes each problem
  report    Write a report of the last failure, with paths and code removed. Nothing is sent
  clean     Delete the cache, or with --all the index too
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --workspace <FILE>  The .code-workspace file to use instead of finding one
      --json              Print one JSON object, {"schema":1,…}, on stdout
  -q, --quiet             Print nothing but errors
      --no-color          No colour, as NO_COLOR does
  -y, --yes               Answer yes to every question; needed for destructive commands without a terminal
  -v, --verbose...        More output on stderr: -v info, -vv debug, -vvv trace
  -h, --help              Print help
  -V, --version           Print version

Every command takes [dir], the current folder by default. Exit codes: 0 done, 1 failed, 2 bad arguments or no workspace, 3 `status --check` found a repo behind.
